menu "Heart Beacon"

    config HB_BTN_GPIO
        int "Button GPIO (active low, internal pull-up)"
        range 0 5
        default 0
        help
            Must be one of GPIO0-5: only those can wake the ESP32-C3 from deep sleep.

    config HB_LED_PWR_GPIO
        int "LED rail load-switch GPIO, -1 = none"
        range -1 21
        default -1
        help
            -1 on carrier rev A (LEDs always powered). Rev B drives a high-side switch from GPIO10 (plan M9);
            that driver is not written yet, so any other value fails the build.

    config HB_HAS_XTAL32K
        bool "32 kHz crystal fitted"
        default n
        help
            The SuperMini has none. A crystal occupies GPIO0/1 and needs RTC_CLK_SRC_EXT_CRYS.

    config HB_LED_WS2811_400K
        bool "LED timing: true 400 kHz (WS2811)"
        default n
        help
            n: the waveform v1 actually sends. v1 asks Adafruit NeoPixel for NEO_KHZ400, but on
            arduino-esp32 3.x (IDF 5) the library's esp.c ignores the speed flag and always sends
            0.4/0.8 us symbols (1.2 us per bit). y: the 400 kHz WS2811 timing (0.5/2.0 and 1.2/1.3 us)
            the library used on IDF 4. Switch only if the bench shows wrong colours.

    config HB_BENCH_FAST_NAP
        bool "Bench: nap after 1 min idle, wake every 1 min"
        default n
        help
            Overrides pwr.idle_nap_min and pwr.nap_wake_min so the bench can see NAP, the timer wake and
            the button wake in minutes. Never ship with this on.

endmenu
